        </register>
        <register>
          <name>GPIOC_LCKR</name>
          <displayName>GPIO port configuration lock register</displayName>
          <description>This register is used to lock the configuration of the port bits when a correct write sequence is applied to bit 16 (LCKK). The value of bits [15:0] is used to lock the configuration of the GPIO.
During the write sequence, LCKR[15:0] value must not change. When the LOCK sequence has been applied on a port bit, the value of this port bit can no longer be modified until the next MCU reset or peripheral reset.
Each lock bit freezes corresponding configuration bits in configuration and alternate function registers.
Individual bits of this register are protected against nonsecure access when corresponding SECy = 1 in GPIO_SECCFGR and the system is secure (TZEN = 1).</description>
          <addressOffset>0x1C</addressOffset>
          <size>32</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>LCK0</name>
              <description>Port x I/O pin y lock
These bits are read/write but can only be written when LCKK = 0.
Note: This bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value when the corresponding I/O is not available on the selected package.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>Port configuration not locked</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>Port configuration locked</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>LCK1</name>
